## 7. Data Availability

### Raw Data — Availability Following Manuscript Acceptance

**The raw data underlying this study are not publicly available at the current stage of manuscript preparation and submission.**

The research dataset is being retained while the associated manuscript is prepared for submission to *New Phytologist*.

**The authors intend to make the complete raw dataset publicly available following acceptance of the associated manuscript.**

Upon acceptance, the data will be deposited in an appropriate research data repository, and the corresponding access information and persistent identifier will be added to this GitHub repository and to the manuscript's Data Availability Statement.

The publicly released dataset is intended to support independent verification, reproducibility, and future comparative research.

During editorial evaluation and peer review, underlying materials required for scientific assessment may be made available confidentially to the editors and reviewers, subject to the applicable journal policies.

### Code Availability

The R scripts developed for the analytical workflow are publicly available in this repository.

The code documents the implemented statistical methods, phylogenetic analyses, model comparisons, and figure-generation procedures.

However, because the original input dataset is not currently included, **full independent reproduction of the analyses is not yet possible using the public repository alone**.

Following data release, the authors intend to provide the information necessary to link the research dataset and analytical code.

The final data-sharing arrangements will comply with the applicable policies of *New Phytologist*.

